<title>NETHERLANDS: Goldman Sachs raises ABN AMRO EPS.</title>
<headline>Goldman Sachs raises ABN AMRO EPS.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of Jan 16 research.</p>
<p>Company---------Sector--------Price---Broker----------------</p>
<p>ABN AMRO	  Banking	 117.60  Goldman Sachs</p>
<p>COMMENT: Standard Federal acquisition and MeesPierson sale will have positive effect on earnings stream but only modest impact on EPS. Shares are fully valued on valuation methodology. We retain our market performer rating on the shares.</p>
<p>    Estimates (Dfl):   EPS	pvs	P/E     Dividend</p>
<p>    1995 (actual)	7.70     ---     15.3	3.60</p>
<p>    1996		   9.33     9.02    12.6</p>
<p>    1997		   9.68     9.25    12.1</p>
<p>Note: Shares were at 120.70 guilders at 1420 GMT today, and Goldman Sachs analyst Neil Crowder said he maintained the rating.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (Fax +31 20 504 5040)</p>
